cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Portugal Minimum Wage, Productivity and Inflation: a reproducible
  exposure-based analysis
message: >-
  If you use this software or the accompanying analysis, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Diogo
    family-names: Ribeiro
    email: diogo_dj@hotmail.com
    # Add your ORCID once available:
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/DiogoRibeiro7/portugal-minimum-wage-inflation'
abstract: >-
  Reproducible research repository studying the interaction between Portugal's
  statutory minimum wage, labour productivity, and consumer-price inflation from
  the introduction of the national minimum wage in 1974 to the present. The
  analysis combines long-run macro accounting with an exposure-based panel
  local-projection design that links statutory wage shocks to the CPI/HICP
  categories most exposed to minimum-wage labour costs.
keywords:
  - minimum wage
  - inflation
  - pass-through
  - labour productivity
  - Portugal
  - local projections
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
license-url: 'https://github.com/DiogoRibeiro7/portugal-minimum-wage-inflation/blob/main/LICENSE'
version: 0.1.0
